# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feather & Bone web client — environment template.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
# Never put secrets here: everything in this file ships to the client.
#
# In particular: NO Cloudinary API secret, no SMTP password, no database URI,
# no payment credentials. Those belong to the backend and stay there.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the API lives, INCLUDING the /api/v1 prefix.
#
# Development: the value below. Vite also proxies /api and /uploads to port 7000,
# so cookies stay first-party while you work.
#
# PRODUCTION MUST NOT BE LOCALHOST. The bundle is served to the customer's
# browser, so `localhost` means *their* machine — every request fails and the
# site loads but does nothing. Set this in the hosting dashboard (Vercel:
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables) to the real API origin, e.g.
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.featherbone.com/api/v1
#
# It is read at BUILD time, not run time: change it and redeploy, or the old
# value stays baked into the bundle.
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Production does not use this file — the deployed
# value lives in .env.production, which Vite reads for `npm run build`:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://backend.featherbonepk.com/api/v1
#
# Leaving this blank also works locally: the client falls back to a relative
# /api/v1, which the dev server proxies to port 7000.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:7000/api/v1

VITE_APP_NAME=Feather & Bone
VITE_CURRENCY=PKR
